nistrator's Guide.  All our recommendations about developing applications, some of which used to be part of the Best Practices as well, have been consolidated in the SAP BTP Developer’s Guide.   This restructuring aims to ensure that both developers and administrators can easily find relevant and specialized guidance.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2144 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2024.21\nDescription: New and changed features are available for administration, data cataloging, data integration, data modeling, and space management.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2024.21. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2145 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changes to the SAP Document AI Basic UI\nDescription: We’ve made a number of enhancements to the SAP Document AI basic UI.       When you upload a document and choose it on the Documents screen, you now see the extraction results for header fields and line items alongside the document preview, without first having to click Extraction Results.      In the extraction results, you can now use the filters at the top of the Edit pane to set which extraction confidence ranges to display. You can select either a single range or all of them.      When using the Template feature, you can now edit and confirm extraction results for the associated document by choosing it on the details page for the template you've created.      Also on the Template details page, you can now set an extraction method for individual fields or for all fields your template. The available methods are Template and AI.      See View and Edit Extraction Results, Add Documents and Activate/Deactivate Template, and Add Template.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2146 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Factur-X and ZUGFeRD Standards - Support for Version 2.3\nDescription: SAP Document AI now supports the version 2.3 of e-invoice document files in Factur-X and ZUGFeRD standards.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2147 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Instant Learning for Information Extraction Using Generative AI (Premium Edition)\nDescription: SAP Document AI now allows you to enhance extraction with generative AI by using your edited extraction results to enrich the prompt to large language models (LLMs) with user feedback.  If you use an appropriately configured schema, SAP Document AI learns from your feedback as soon you commit documents with edited extraction results. As a result, information extraction is improved for relevant fields in all subsequent documents.  To use this feature, you must first activate it using the configuration key enableInstantLearning.  See Instant Learning (Premium Edition) and Configuration Keys.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-22\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2148 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New List of Values Data Type for Schemas (Premium Edition)\nDescription: With SAP Document AI you can now use the data type list of values to extract header or line item fields with the setup type auto.  The new data type allows you to define multiple values for fields. For example, if your company handles three different types of invoice, you can define these as list values. As a result, only these values are extracted for Invoice Type fields in your documents. \",8530\n60,\"--- Record 4141 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Define Custom Variables for Your Process\nDescription: You can define variables that are available on a global level of the process. That is, these variables do not stem from a previous process activity. You use them to provide input, for example, for an activity that follows conditional branches.  See Configure Process Variables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-28\nValid as Of: 2023-09-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4142 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Input Validation in Forms\nDescription: In the form editor, you can configure input validation for the text fields in the form you create. For more information, see Form Input Fields.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-28\nValid as Of: 2023-09-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4143 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Interface com.sap.xsa.security.container.XSUserInfo has been deprecated\nDescription: With SAP Java Buildpack 1.77.0, component xs-user-holder is changed due to deprecated code in SAP BTP Security Services Integration Libraries, on which it relies.  Interface com.sap.xsa.security.container.XSUserInfo was deprecated and later removed with version 3.0.0 of cloud-security-services-integration-library. For more information, see: SAP BTP Security Services Integration Libraries: v 3.0.0  This interface is replaced by a new one – com.sap.xs.security.UserData. It's introduced with version 1.47.0 of xs-user-holder.   If your pom.xml file contains the following <dependency>, that means your project uses xs-user-holder and needs to be adapted:   <dependency>\n    <groupId>com.sap.cloud.sjb</groupId>\n    <artifactId>xs-user-holder</artifactId>\n</dependency>\n  The xs-user-holder component currently provides getter and setter methods for working with the deprecated com.sap.xsa.security.container.XSUserInfo.   Action: If your code uses these methods, make the following modifications:      Replace UserInfoHolder.getUserInfo() with UserInfoHolder.getUserData()      Replace UserInfoHolder.setUserInfo(XSUserInfo userInfo) with UserInfoHolder.setUserData(UserData userData)      Note      The same token information that XSUserInfo provides can be obtained with the new UserData interface.      Getter and setter methods for the deprecated com.sap.xsa.security.container.XSUserInfo will remain available in the xs-user-holder component, and will coexist with the methods from com.sap.xs.security.UserData till December 31, 2023.      When this period is over, everything based on the deprecated code from package com.sap.xsa.security.container will be removed, and only the new UserData interface will be supported in the xs-user-holder component.    \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-15\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4144 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Corporate IdP\nDescription: Identity Authentication added new parameter idp which allows sign in to specific application with specific corporate identity provider. See Configure the Client to Call Identity Authentication Authorize Endpoint for Authorization Code Flowand Configure IdP-Initiated SSO.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-28\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4145 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-28\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4146 ---\nComponent: Cloud Management Tools,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Directory Enhancements for Managing Users and Entitlements\nDescription: Directories are primarily used for grouping your subaccounts, but they can also be used to manage their own entitlements and users. Previously, enabling the entitlement and user management features for a directory was only possible after the directory was created, from the directory's Users and Entitlements pages.   Now, we've made it easier for you to enable these features right from the start when you create a directory, or when editing a directory from the Account Explorer page.  Furthermore, we've added the ability to enable the entitlement management feature for any directory directly on the global account's Entitlements  Entity Entitlements page. Until now, this page did not allow you to select directories that weren't enabled to manage entitlements. Now, these directories can be selected.  For more information, see Entitlements and Quotas, Create a Directory, Configure Entitlements and Quotas for Directories, and Manage Users in Directories.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-09-27\nValid as Of: 2023-09-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4147 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enh\",8364\n270,\"--- Record 2001 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Unified View\nDescription: Try out the new unified view that is replacing the explore and manage views on your AvS instance. To access the unified view, append /evaluations to 